1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,403
Imagine this. Your car breaks down,

2
00:00:02,303 --> 00:00:03,662
and the mechanic says:

3
00:00:03,562 --> 00:00:04,864
four hundred dollars.

4
00:00:05,114 --> 00:00:06,661
Could you pay that right now,

5
00:00:06,561 --> 00:00:07,608
in cash? Be honest.

6
00:00:07,858 --> 00:00:09,144
If the answer is no,

7
00:00:09,044 --> 00:00:10,211
you are not alone.

8
00:00:10,111 --> 00:00:11,100
Not even close.

9
00:00:11,350 --> 00:00:13,306
More than a third of American adults

10
00:00:13,206 --> 00:00:16,192
couldn't cover a four hundred dollar surprise with cash.

11
00:00:16,442 --> 00:00:18,294
So today, I'll show you how to

12
00:00:18,194 --> 00:00:19,695
build an emergency fund,

13
00:00:19,595 --> 00:00:21,155
even on a small paycheck.

14
00:00:21,405 --> 00:00:23,219
Here's what happens without one.

15
00:00:23,119 --> 00:00:25,790
Every surprise goes straight onto a credit card.

16
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:28,250
Then the interest makes next month even

17
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:29,928
tighter. And the cycle repeats.

18
00:00:30,178 --> 00:00:32,375
It's not because you're bad with money.

19
00:00:32,275 --> 00:00:33,826
Life is just unpredictable.

20
00:00:34,076 --> 00:00:36,422
An emergency fund is the wall between

21
00:00:36,322 --> 00:00:37,453
you and new debt.

22
00:00:37,703 --> 00:00:39,805
You've heard you need six months of

23
00:00:39,705 --> 00:00:41,635
expenses saved. On a low income,

24
00:00:41,535 --> 00:00:42,893
that feels impossible.

25
00:00:43,143 --> 00:00:44,514
So forget that for now.

26
00:00:44,414 --> 00:00:47,001
Your first goal is just five hundred dollars.

27
00:00:47,251 --> 00:00:49,122
That alone covers a car repair,

28
00:00:49,022 --> 00:00:50,208
a new phone screen,

29
00:00:50,108 --> 00:00:51,293
or a surprise bill.

30
00:00:51,543 --> 00:00:54,071
Hit it? Great. Now aim for one thousand.

31
00:00:54,321 --> 00:00:57,097
Step two. Find the money that's already slipping away.

32
00:00:57,347 --> 00:00:59,115
Subscriptions you forgot about.

33
00:00:59,015 --> 00:01:00,190
Apps you never open.

34
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:02,795
Overdraft fees. Monthly account fees.

35
00:01:02,695 --> 00:01:05,172
Many banks offer accounts without them.

36
00:01:05,422 --> 00:01:07,383
And those little daily extras.

37
00:01:07,283 --> 00:01:09,617
Snacks, delivery fees, impulse buys.

38
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:11,840
Just sixty dollars a month is seven

39
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:13,660
hundred and twenty dollars a year!

40
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:15,855
Step three. Pick an amount you can

41
00:01:15,755 --> 00:01:17,103
save every single week,

42
00:01:17,003 --> 00:01:18,188
no matter how small.

43
00:01:18,438 --> 00:01:20,575
Ten dollars a week becomes five hundred

44
00:01:20,475 --> 00:01:22,090
and twenty dollars in a year.

45
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:23,437
Twenty five a week?

46
00:01:23,337 --> 00:01:24,697
That's thirteen hundred.

47
00:01:24,947 --> 00:01:27,288
Fifty a week? Twenty six hundred dollars!

48
00:01:27,538 --> 00:01:29,823
The amount matters less than the habit.

49
00:01:29,723 --> 00:01:31,393
Consistency builds the fund.

50
00:01:31,643 --> 00:01:34,439
Step four. Take willpower out of the game completely.

51
00:01:34,689 --> 00:01:37,863
Set up an automatic transfer to savings on payday.

52
00:01:38,113 --> 00:01:40,292
Many banks let you split your direct

53
00:01:40,192 --> 00:01:42,602
deposit, so part of every paycheck lands

54
00:01:42,502 --> 00:01:43,815
in savings by itself.

55
00:01:44,065 --> 00:01:45,829
Money you never see in checking is

56
00:01:45,729 --> 00:01:46,906
money you won't spend.

57
00:01:47,156 --> 00:01:49,511
Step five. Where you keep this money matters.

58
00:01:49,761 --> 00:01:51,706
If it sits in your checking account,

59
00:01:51,606 --> 00:01:53,142
it will disappear. Trust me.

60
00:01:53,392 --> 00:01:55,606
Put it in a separate savings account,

61
00:01:55,506 --> 00:01:58,007
ideally high yield, at a federally insured

62
00:01:57,907 --> 00:01:59,207
bank or credit union.

63
00:01:59,457 --> 00:02:00,645
And don't invest it.

64
00:02:00,545 --> 00:02:01,788
It needs to be there,

65
00:02:01,688 --> 00:02:03,857
at full value, the moment you need it.

66
00:02:04,107 --> 00:02:05,459
Want to get there faster?

67
00:02:05,359 --> 00:02:07,614
Use money that isn't part of your paycheck.

68
00:02:07,864 --> 00:02:09,956
A tax refund can fill your starter

69
00:02:09,856 --> 00:02:11,186
fund in a single day.

70
00:02:11,436 --> 00:02:12,891
A few hours of side work.

71
00:02:12,791 --> 00:02:14,843
Selling stuff you don't use anymore.

72
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:16,894
Rule of thumb: send at least half

73
00:02:16,794 --> 00:02:19,112
of any surprise money straight to the fund.

74
00:02:19,362 --> 00:02:21,634
Step seven. Decide ahead of time what

75
00:02:21,534 --> 00:02:22,984
counts as an emergency.

76
00:02:23,234 --> 00:02:25,248
A car repair you need for work,

77
00:02:25,148 --> 00:02:27,531
a medical bill, losing your job? Yes.

78
00:02:27,781 --> 00:02:29,221
A big sale, a concert,

79
00:02:29,121 --> 00:02:30,378
a holiday trip? No.

80
00:02:30,278 --> 00:02:32,387
Those get their own savings goal.

81
00:02:32,637 --> 00:02:33,612
And if you use it?

82
00:02:33,512 --> 00:02:35,264
That's okay. That's what it's for.

83
00:02:35,164 --> 00:02:36,431
Just start refilling it.

84
00:02:36,681 --> 00:02:38,130
Here's the full roadmap.

85
00:02:38,030 --> 00:02:40,323
First, five hundred. Then one thousand.

86
00:02:40,573 --> 00:02:42,537
Then three months of essentials:

87
00:02:42,437 --> 00:02:44,459
rent, food, utilities, transport.

88
00:02:44,709 --> 00:02:46,362
And over time, six months.

89
00:02:46,262 --> 00:02:48,751
Every stage makes you safer than before.

90
00:02:49,001 --> 00:02:50,697
You don't need a big income to

91
00:02:50,597 --> 00:02:51,707
build a safety net.

92
00:02:51,607 --> 00:02:52,930
You just need to start.

93
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:55,377
If this helped, subscribe for one simple

94
00:02:55,277 --> 00:02:56,478
money move every day.

95
00:02:56,728 --> 00:02:58,128
And tell me in the comments:

96
00:02:58,028 --> 00:02:59,568
what's your first savings goal?
